    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282-a2">

                <pb facs="0675" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg579"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 2 in No. 187.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 24,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your dispatch dated the 19th, and received on the 24th instant, and
                    to tender you therefor my thanks.</p>
                <p>It is certainly gratifying to learn of the progress which “Le Comité d’Ordre
                    Public” is making in maintaining peace and good order in the communtity, and in
                    advancing and preserving the general interest.</p>
                <p>Hoping that all relations which I am called to sustain with your country may be
                    in future, as in the past, altogether pleasant,</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MERCER LANGSTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Denis</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >President</hi>, and <hi rendition="#small-caps">Délorme</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Vice-President</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Le
                            Comité d’Ordre Public.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
